body:
This is probably a known issue, but I could not find any issues nor documents related to it. Feel free to close this ticket if it's duplicate or already discussed.

## Repro

Run `cargo init --lib` in a random directory and add the following code as `src/lib.rs`.

```rust
pub struct Foo {
    pub i: i32,
}

impl Foo {
    pub const fn new(i: i32) -> Self {
        Foo { i }
    }
}

#[cfg(test)]
mod tests {
    use super::*;

    #[test]
    fn it_works() {
        let foo = const { Foo::new(42) };
        assert_eq!(foo.i, 42);
    }
}
```

And run

```sh
cargo llvm-cov --html
```

## Expected behavior

`Foo::new` is correctly measured as it is called in `it_works` test case.

## Actual behavior

`Foo::new` is not covered so it is not measured correctly. This result is not surprising because the function is actually not run at runtime but run at compile time. I guess fixing this issue is hard because LLVM doesn't know which lines were executed by rustc's constant expression evaluator. However at least it would be nice to mention this in the [Known Limitation section](https://github.com/taiki-e/cargo-llvm-cov#known-limitations).

